WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:04.180
We have a special emphasis on
the unique challenges that women face.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.510
When they try to negotiate, when they try
to manage teams, when they try to lead.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:11.140
&gt;&gt; Some people find it very
difficult to be authoritative,

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:12.410
even when the roll calls for that.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:15.330
Some people find it very difficult
to ever deffer to anyone.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.980
There's a lot of research that
indicates that women just don't

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:20.720
choose to negotiate in
circumstances where men do.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.541
And this has tremendous implications.

00:00:22.541 --> 00:00:29.615
[MUSIC]

00:00:29.615 --> 00:00:33.090
I try to expand their expectations
about what is negotiation

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:36.160
beyond an adversarial
win-lose kind of dynamic.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.430
We have them negotiate, and
I use their results as the basis for

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:45.620
the discussion for developing a framework
for how can they be more effective.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:48.910
&gt;&gt; What we deal with in this course
is understanding the psychology

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:50.820
that gets in the way of
feeling comfortable.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.470
The opportunity to step back and

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:56.610
think in a more big picture kind of
way about our goals, our aspirations.

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:59.980
The extent to which we contribute
to the bottom line in our company.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.930
&gt;&gt; One thing that came to my mind
during this last week was this whole

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:04.240
idea about power.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:07.590
The power in silence,
the power in not acting.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:11.460
&gt;&gt; The thing that both Debby and Maggie
always retreated one knows these things.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.350
It's just a matter of seeing it
from a different perspective.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.440
I would recommend this program
just to have a confirmation,

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.160
is your leadership style okay?

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.050
Do you need to make any improvements?

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:23.000
&gt;&gt; We provide them with specific
strategies for dealing with the problems

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:27.020
that they face, and they're like,
I wish I'd had this years ago.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.750
This has transformed how I
think about this problem.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:33.950
&gt;&gt; And it's very cool when faculty members
hear that we have transformed your lives.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.182
It's kind of like, yes,
this is what we're here for.

00:01:36.182 --> 00:01:37.664
[MUSIC]

